From 905d1ca53e302c8cf6187975598576d2a6a6501b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 20:17:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] shared: add inert no-DPI stubs for blob-referenced bwdpi
 symbols

With RTCONFIG_BWDPI off, the whole body of shared/bwdpi_utils.c compiles
out and -lbwdpi is dropped, but the closed blobs amas_lib.o (AMAS) and
nt_mail.o (Notification Center) still reference check_wrs_switch,
check_bwdpi_nvram_setting, check_tdts_module_exist and get_fw_user_list
(httpd web.c also calls check_tdts_module_exist) -> rc link failed with
exactly these four undefined. Add an #else branch with inert stubs that
report the DPI engine as disabled/not present (0 / 0 / 0 / -1). With
BWDPI on the real implementations take over; the stubs vanish.

Same pattern as the Phase-1.1 add_ifttt_flag blob dependency.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/shared/bwdpi_utils.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/shared/bwdpi_utils.c b/release/src/router/shared/bwdpi_utils.c
index 6251533ca2..1cc71b0eff 100644
--- a/release/src/router/shared/bwdpi_utils.c
+++ b/release/src/router/shared/bwdpi_utils.c
@@ -221,6 +221,31 @@ void tm_recycle_stuck_process()
 		}
 	}
 }
+#else
+/* inert stubs: the closed blobs amas_lib.o / nt_mail.o (and web.c) still
+ * reference these when the DPI engine is compiled out; real versions live
+ * above / in libbwdpi. All report "disabled / not present". */
+int check_wrs_switch()
+{
+	return 0;
+}
+
+int check_bwdpi_nvram_setting()
+{
+	return 0;
+}
+
+int check_tdts_module_exist()
+{
+	return 0;
+}
+
+int get_fw_user_list(void *output, unsigned int *used_len)
+{
+	(void)output;
+	(void)used_len;
+	return -1;
+}
 #endif
 
